WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.480
- The Voice has been on for 17 seasons,

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.030
so my first question obviously had to go

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.520
to the two that have been
here since the beginning.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.680
I mean, from the first season,

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.960
what do you think has changed the most?

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.687
- Well, Blake's hair is much grayer.

00:00:14.687 --> 00:00:15.780
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.490
That's just for starters,
off the top of my head.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.140
- And I've added this third chin.

00:00:20.861 --> 00:00:22.754
- I found one of those too!

00:00:22.754 --> 00:00:23.660
(all laughing)

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:24.493
- You know, we never thought this show,

00:00:24.493 --> 00:00:25.673
people thought we were
crazy, and I say "we"

00:00:25.673 --> 00:00:27.660
because I think I was the
first hire on the show

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.190
when NBC came to us

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.710
and myself and Adam Levine both,

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.290
were not huge Idol
watchers, I was in radio,

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.020
I worked at KROQ here in
Los Angeles, I was at MTV.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:37.853
- Yeah.

00:00:37.853 --> 00:00:39.450
- And these shows on TV
where people were singing,

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:43.830
at the time, don't have the
credibility that they have now.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:44.663
- No.

00:00:44.663 --> 00:00:47.160
- So getting The Voice, when
we watched the tape of it,

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.690
it was happening in another country

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.330
and it was beating Idol and
X-Factor and all these shows.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.060
We really liked the idea
of coaches helping people

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:54.893
and not just coaches,

00:00:54.893 --> 00:00:56.370
but the best in the best in the business.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.410
So just from the conception of the show,

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.410
the idea was warm and it
seemed like mentoring, helping.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.550
And those are the themes that I think

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.650
has helped the show last for 17 seasons.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.930
In Idol, if one of your judges left,

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.730
it was like, "Oh, there's
trouble in paradise!"

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.260
You know, "Simon's leaving!"

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.820
It was like drama, but
for us, it was like,

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.940
well, of course Shakira's
gonna go, she's got a tour.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:15.773
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:15.773 --> 00:01:16.606
- So I think our rotating chairs

00:01:16.606 --> 00:01:18.177
has helped the show last long too.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:19.570
- And yeah, it's always fun
to see different artists.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:20.820
- [Carson] Yeah.
- Yeah, of course.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:21.900
- We've had some great ones too.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.110
- Yeah, what's different
for you, coaching wise?

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.550
'Cause you, I'm gonna brag on you,

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.350
and I do this all the time when I say

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.200
you really do help people afterward.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.830
And from that first season
you have been so helpful

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.920
to all the artists afterwards,
and it's a lot of time.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:41.280
- Well, I think you gotta
draw the line somewhere,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.180
at some point, you know?

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.300
And I think what I've found
for me over the years,

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.850
there's just some people that you have

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:51.330
a stronger connection
with, obviously, in life,

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:52.560
and I meet so many people,

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.020
I was talking backstage a while ago,

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.721
I think I've worked with over
200 artists now on the show.

00:01:58.721 --> 00:02:00.420
- Oh my gosh, that's crazy!

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.923
- And they all live with
him, which is weird!

00:02:02.923 --> 00:02:03.756
- Yeah.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.310
- That's the line that I'm talking about.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.143
I literally.

00:02:06.143 --> 00:02:06.976
- Line in the sand.

00:02:06.976 --> 00:02:08.913
- They can't shower with you but.

00:02:10.065 --> 00:02:10.898
- He literally does though.

00:02:10.898 --> 00:02:13.110
He has it like a youth hostel in Oklahoma

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.530
where all the past contestants
all live in his back house.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:17.363
He's too kind.

00:02:17.363 --> 00:02:19.950
- It started to feel that way for a while.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.830
After the first season I was a coach,

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.050
I think I probably lost money.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.111
- You probably did.

00:02:26.111 --> 00:02:28.477
- You try to do stuff for people.

00:02:28.477 --> 00:02:30.673
- You were like paying
for apartments for a year

00:02:30.673 --> 00:02:32.100
and it was crazy.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.764
- Wow, join Team Blake.

00:02:33.764 --> 00:02:35.884
(all laughing)

00:02:35.884 --> 00:02:39.535
I am not willing to offer
all the perks that he is.

00:02:39.535 --> 00:02:41.970
- The cool thing about the show is

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.980
you get to work with
people outside of genres

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.840
that you really sing
in and you perform in.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.250
And that's what I love about it.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.360
What has it taught you?

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.890
Like Blake you're in country music,

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:53.550
but you've been working
with people in soulful pop,

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:54.930
like all different kinds of genres.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:55.920
What has that kind of taught you

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.120
about different genres of music?

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.337
- Speaking of the first
season, I remember thinking,

00:02:59.337 --> 00:03:03.120
cause I had, remember Dia Frampton was on

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.470
and she was wanting to do all that.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.553
I was thinking like,

00:03:06.427 --> 00:03:08.070
oh she's wanting to do
some pop stuff, you know?

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.230
I'll get some Billy Ocean.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:11.063
- Right.

00:03:11.063 --> 00:03:11.896
- Something like that, you know.

00:03:11.896 --> 00:03:14.220
That's what in my mind,
oh, some Cindy Lauper,

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.840
that's what we're gonna

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.670
and then she's wanting
to do all these people

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.740
like Kanye West, what?

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.270
Like, what are you talking?

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.410
Who's that, when is that?

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.618
When did that come out, you know?

00:03:24.618 --> 00:03:28.590
And so, first season was just a huge

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.210
learning curve for me, you know?

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.290
And it changed.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.123
- Well you won with Jermaine,

00:03:32.123 --> 00:03:33.090
was it second season?

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:37.740
- Yeah, I think it was, it
changes also the records

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.600
that you make as an artist, you know,

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.940
cause you start becoming
exposed to all this other stuff.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:43.645
That's why I rap now.

00:03:43.645 --> 00:03:44.478
(all laughing)

00:03:44.478 --> 00:03:45.311
- Exactly.

00:03:45.311 --> 00:03:46.803
- Learning who Kanye was, yeah.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.560
I do think it has some effect though.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.580
- [Gwen] For sure.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.170
- Yeah, what about you
like working with honors?

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.003
You never thought you.

00:03:53.003 --> 00:03:55.770
- This is the thing, going
off of what you said about the

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:59.100
time period of where, when
my band came out and what we,

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.640
how we like just evolved in the
TV shows and all that stuff.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.000
I think that I just didn't even
know anything about the show

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.200
when I joined it,

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.310
but it has been one of the
most inspirational things that

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.170
I've ever done in my entire career.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.910
And I've already been alive a long time.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:17.820
So it's been like a major, I mean,

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:21.048
because it's not only are
you playing a different role,

00:04:21.048 --> 00:04:23.280
you know, like it's this kind
of coaching motherly role.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.160
It's also like you're exposed
to all this different music.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.728
You're hearing it in like
through different voices

00:04:29.728 --> 00:04:31.980
and you're like looking
up music all the time.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.500
So you're seeing and
hearing music so much.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.510
So it's really, it's very, very like,

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.700
it affects you as an artist.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:39.533
- Yeah.

00:04:39.533 --> 00:04:41.310
- And then you get to sit
next to John legend and,

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:42.153
and he's like.

00:04:43.208 --> 00:04:44.041
It's crazy.

00:04:44.041 --> 00:04:45.330
- Sexy.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.500
- Sexiness man alive.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.162
- I think we're aware.

00:04:48.162 --> 00:04:50.710
- I'm between so much
sexiness, look at me.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:51.784
Oh.

00:04:51.784 --> 00:04:52.746
(all laughing)

00:04:52.746 --> 00:04:54.160
I don't know what to do.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.360
- So what about, okay, sexiest man alive,

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.860
what has it done for you?

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.390
Because you also came
from a choir background

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:01.260
where you were kind of exposed

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.760
to a lot of different music probably too.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.170
- I was exposed to a
lot of different music,

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.030
but it really is fun doing this.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.240
I think people don't
realize how much fun it is

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.555
to coach other artists.

00:05:10.555 --> 00:05:11.388
- Yeah.

00:05:11.388 --> 00:05:14.580
- I did use to direct
choirs when I was younger

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.920
and I was a minister
of music at my church.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:21.720
But this coaching aspect, I
haven't really done since then

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:25.260
and doing that for, you
know, 12 artists, 10 artists,

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:26.700
whatever we have that season.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.770
It's really fun, it's really exciting.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.510
But it's also a little bit heartbreaking

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.640
cause you have to let
people go so quickly.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:33.473
- Yeah.

00:05:33.473 --> 00:05:35.220
- And like we pick 12 people for our team.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.060
We're so excited.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.950
We try to convince all 12 of them to come

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:41.610
and then a week later we're
like, bye to half of them.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.540
And it's really hard

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.590
because you already get attached to them.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:46.947
You're inspired by them.

00:05:46.947 --> 00:05:48.060
- You see their potential.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.110
- Yeah, you see their potential

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:51.210
and then you have to let
people go so quickly.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.640
- Yeah, that freaked me out
the first season I did it.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.290
But then the producers kept reminding me,

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:56.220
they know what they're signing up for

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:57.420
and you know what, I'm one of those kids

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.740
and you do know what
you're signing up for.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:05:59.573
- Yeah.

00:05:59.573 --> 00:06:00.406
- That everybody's getting off it.

00:06:00.406 --> 00:06:01.239
- Also it's like one of those things

00:06:01.239 --> 00:06:03.000
where we're all on a journey,

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.050
we're all going home

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.390
and it's all just a moment
in our life journey.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:07.740
And so if you look at it like that,

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.990
it's just an amazing thing
that you're going through

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:10.860
in that moment,

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:13.680
you're gonna always have to
move on to something else.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.420
- It's a good lesson to
learn like right off the bat.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:16.253
- It is true.

00:06:16.253 --> 00:06:17.086
- Yes and we all deal

00:06:17.086 --> 00:06:18.900
with rejection in our business.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:19.733
- [Kelly] Never.

00:06:21.366 --> 00:06:23.610
- We've dealt with it from
the beginning of our careers

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.220
and we've gotten to this place
and we're very fortunate.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.800
But even now we still deal with rejection.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:29.633
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:06:29.633 --> 00:06:30.599
- Yes.

00:06:30.599 --> 00:06:32.370
- Yeah, I'm just kidding.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.570
This season has been so fun.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.860
I cannot wait for everybody
to see these blinds.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:39.420
Cause I feel like since you
are sitting next to Blake,

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:43.110
you two, the banter is so funny.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.970
You give him crap right back.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.130
And not a lot of people hang there.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.770
- I learned that you have
to preempt his crap giving.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:51.900
- Oh my gosh, you nailed it.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:53.040
- Just jump him, beat him to it.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:54.810
- Gosh, it was good.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:55.894
- It's been a lot of fun.

00:06:55.894 --> 00:06:57.900
- It was literally my favorite
blinds we've ever shot.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:58.733
- Really?

00:06:58.733 --> 00:06:59.702
- Yeah, I told the producers, I was like,

00:06:59.702 --> 00:07:02.400
it felt like I was
getting paid to have fun.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.260
Like I was like, this is awesome.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:07.430
I was going home at night and
I was like, I love my jobs.

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:09.030
So your second run on
The Voice starts tonight.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.590
So how are you feeling this time?

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:13.560
You feel like way more
relaxed about giving us crap,

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:14.490
which I love.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:18.539
- I now view all of you as
like my brothers and sister.

00:07:18.539 --> 00:07:19.590
- [Kelly] Exactly.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.330
- And so I don't really care.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:22.163
I'm just gonna --

00:07:22.163 --> 00:07:22.996
- No one has feelings.

00:07:22.996 --> 00:07:23.829
- Let, let it go.

00:07:23.829 --> 00:07:26.490
And just, just take you guys down a notch.

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:27.360
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.193
- No, it's been fun.

00:07:28.193 --> 00:07:30.120
I honestly love doing
the show with you guys

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:33.000
and working with these incredible artists,

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.680
but I learned a lot from
the first season, you know,

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.963
and just interacting with them.

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:39.000
We're coaches, sure,

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.620
but I think the thing
that's so cool is that

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:43.500
we also learn so much in
the process about ourselves

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.378
and the artists we're working with

00:07:45.378 --> 00:07:46.590
and how to give each other crap.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:49.020
And that's been the most
fun and rewarding part

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.640
of being on the show for a second season.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:52.530
- Well, because you have
to navigate the person.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:53.610
Because all the coaches are different.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.950
You're like, how far can I push this one?

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.020
- Well, that was the first
thing on like day one

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.070
of my first season.

00:07:59.070 --> 00:07:59.903
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:59.903 --> 00:08:02.160
- [Nick] I didn't know if I
was going to offend someone.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:02.993
There's always that line.

00:08:02.993 --> 00:08:03.826
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:08:03.826 --> 00:08:06.319
- [Nick] But then I realized
you guys are hard to offend.

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:09.120
- It takes an awful lot to offend me.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.560
And usually when people are offensive,

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.563
if it's at least funny, I'm like, points.

00:08:12.563 --> 00:08:13.396
- [Nick] Okay.

00:08:13.396 --> 00:08:14.229
- All right.

00:08:14.229 --> 00:08:15.062
- Yeah, there's been a few things.

00:08:15.062 --> 00:08:16.260
I can't remember exactly which things,

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.370
but times where it was like,

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.110
oh that stung a little bit too much.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.490
- Oh man, so my bad,

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:21.450
we'll hug it out when we can after COVID.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:22.283
- [Nick] Yeah, we'll hug it out.

00:08:22.283 --> 00:08:23.544
- Okay.

00:08:23.544 --> 00:08:24.377
- - [Nick] Well we can't.

00:08:24.377 --> 00:08:26.220
- Yeah, we can't now, but afterwards.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.350
Well there's a history of the guys

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:30.540
being named the sexiest man alive.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.581
We've talked about this in
interviews we've all done.

00:08:32.581 --> 00:08:33.664
- It doesn't really make sense.

00:08:33.664 --> 00:08:35.405
(Kelly laughing)

00:08:35.405 --> 00:08:36.867
I mean, if we have to talk about this,

00:08:36.867 --> 00:08:39.660
but Blake Shelton and John Legend,

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:44.190
depending if I ever was
invited into this brotherhood.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.630
- [Kelly] Adam is in it as well.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:46.463
- Adam.

00:08:46.463 --> 00:08:47.296
- [Kelly] He was one of them.

00:08:47.296 --> 00:08:48.129
- [Nick] Makes more sense.

00:08:48.129 --> 00:08:48.962
- [Kelly] Really?

00:08:48.962 --> 00:08:49.795
- [Nick] Makes more sense.

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:50.628
- Those three, okay.

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:56.860
So I think, you know, I would
question the validity of this.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:57.840
- [Kelly] You question it.

00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:59.430
You think they're running out of people?

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.540
- I think they're running out of people.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.045
- Yeah.

00:09:02.045 --> 00:09:04.569
- I think that maybe Blake
paid somebody, you know,

00:09:04.569 --> 00:09:06.830
I don't wanna start rumors here.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:08.140
- He did something for it.

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:10.740
Remind us what you know, your teams get,

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:11.880
you know, mine get a jacket.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:13.623
What does your team get?

00:09:13.623 --> 00:09:17.070
- My team gets a customized song.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:19.680
- Now customized, you mean,
like you just changed the name.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:23.130
- Yeah, changed the name and
what it rhymes with each,

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:24.630
each rendition.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:27.540
- Wait, my favorite one was
the one that you didn't.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.640
There was no other word
to rhyme with it, but.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:32.940
- But the women's body parts, yeah.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.928
And I didn't wanna say it.

00:09:34.928 --> 00:09:38.890
I wanted everyone to know
that I was thinking it,

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:41.340
but I didn't say it and
let their mind do the work.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:42.720
- It was amazing.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:43.553
What do you do?

00:09:43.553 --> 00:09:44.550
Nick's notes, right, the journal?

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:49.170
- I do a journal, which
I think is a great gift.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.320
- [John] Especially if you have pilot pen.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:54.476
- Especially if you have a G2 pilot pen

00:09:54.476 --> 00:09:55.309
that's in my own hand.

00:09:55.309 --> 00:09:57.200
- I'll trade you a jacket for that?

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.450
- [Kelly] You know what, okay.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.760
Blake what do you give them?

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:00.593
Oh, I forgot.

00:10:00.593 --> 00:10:01.426
- Trophies.

00:10:01.426 --> 00:10:03.751
- This, no, oh my gosh.

00:10:03.751 --> 00:10:05.640
(all laughing)

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:06.473
- I set him up!

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:09.543
Whatever.

00:10:09.543 --> 00:10:11.310
- This has been a lot of fun.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:12.732
I'm enjoying this a lot.

00:10:12.732 --> 00:10:14.343
- This year he's not getting
the trophy this year.

00:10:14.343 --> 00:10:16.290
I wanna talk about some
of our favorite moments

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:17.123
from The Voice.

00:10:17.123 --> 00:10:19.020
So mine is obviously
when I win this season.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:20.839
John, what is yours?

00:10:20.839 --> 00:10:24.060
- I didn't know we were
having kind of conjecture.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:24.900
- Yeah, it's all about projection.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:26.700
- As our favorite moment (laughing).

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:32.880
My favorite was when I won
my first season, season 16.

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:33.713
That was pretty cool.

00:10:33.713 --> 00:10:34.950
With Maelyn Jarmon.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:35.783
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:35.783 --> 00:10:36.616
- [John] That was pretty cool.

00:10:36.616 --> 00:10:38.035
- Yeah, I loved winning.

00:10:38.035 --> 00:10:39.862
Who doesn't love it?
- [John] Winning's awesome.

00:10:39.862 --> 00:10:40.695
- What's your favorite?

00:10:40.695 --> 00:10:41.790
- Nick doesn't know what that feels like.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:42.723
- I haven't won.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:44.783
There's that?

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.980
No, my favorite moment.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:47.813
- [John] Awkward.

00:10:47.813 --> 00:10:49.110
- I have a few.

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:53.583
I think back to season 18 when
Blake brought out the puppy.

00:10:54.799 --> 00:10:56.068
- [Kelly] Snowflake.
- [John] Oh yeah.

00:10:56.068 --> 00:10:56.901
- [Kelly] I wanted him.

00:10:56.901 --> 00:10:59.490
- [John] Oh and then you put
it back in the shelter after.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:00.690
- Yeah, well I was honest.

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:02.240
I said what was gonna happen if

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:04.980
whoever that was that didn't pick me.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:06.990
- Yeah, and look what happened.

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:07.823
- They left a mark though.

00:11:07.823 --> 00:11:08.919
You wanted him pretty badly.

00:11:08.919 --> 00:11:09.930
If you don't remember their name.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:12.540
- The fans didn't like that artist either.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.500
- Yeah.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.590
- Cause they let the puppy
go back to the shelter.

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:18.149
Backfired on him.

00:11:18.149 --> 00:11:20.703
Would've won The Voice and saved the dog.

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:25.230
- What's your favorite
moment from this season?

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:27.753
- From this season, so far,

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.820
I mean, Victor, who's fantastic.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:35.700
He was voted through to
the semifinals by the fans

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:38.700
and his first song on the show
during the blind auditions

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:41.730
was my Oscar winning song with Common.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:42.563
- Yeah.

00:11:42.563 --> 00:11:46.353
- Lori and Blake was the
first to turn for Victor.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:52.190
And his pitch was like, you
must really love gospel music.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.568
And he just kept kinda rambling.

00:11:55.568 --> 00:11:57.090
- I associate the word glory with gospel.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:59.550
- He's just rambling and
trying to bond with him.

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:01.290
And I look at you and I'm like,

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:02.460
he doesn't know it's my song.

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:03.705
- [Kelly] He did literally look at me.

00:12:03.705 --> 00:12:04.538
Here's the thing.

00:12:04.538 --> 00:12:05.371
- In my defense, I don't think he's

00:12:05.371 --> 00:12:06.960
ripping out Boys Around Here.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:10.530
- Hey, you have no idea
what I'm playing in my car.

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:11.580
- Hey, no, on a group text,

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:12.900
remember, they were at Christy's,

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:13.740
they were listening to you.

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:15.150
- We were listening.
- [Kelly] They were.

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:15.983
- That was true.

00:12:15.983 --> 00:12:17.310
- Hey and that's why, just so you know,

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:19.380
they're records, they're
vinyl records today

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:20.310
because of that moment,

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:22.680
I gave them your record on vinyl.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:23.809
- Thank you.

00:12:23.809 --> 00:12:24.642
Thank you.

00:12:24.642 --> 00:12:25.475
- Just so he knew your music.

00:12:25.475 --> 00:12:26.784
- And Gloria's not on that album.

00:12:26.784 --> 00:12:27.870
- It's not on that album, that is correct.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:28.703
- I looked on the back of it.

00:12:28.703 --> 00:12:30.210
- It is on the soundtrack to Selma.

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:33.112
- I was like that's John's only damn song.

00:12:33.112 --> 00:12:36.060
(John laughing)

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:39.090
- What's your favorite
moment from this season?

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:40.530
- I've had a couple favorite moments.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.480
I've had a couple favorite performances.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:43.313
- [Kelly] Oh yeah.

00:12:43.313 --> 00:12:45.120
- Actually I think Victor
Solomon's performance

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:46.740
and Dana Monique's from this last week.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.900
- Oh Yeah, Dana was amazing.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:49.957
- That was Free Your Mind, right?

00:12:49.957 --> 00:12:50.790
- [John] Free Your Mind.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:52.500
Yeah, that was incredible.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.860
- You know, also Dana
Monique, her journey,

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:58.800
her story of kind of coming
from being a background singer,

00:12:58.800 --> 00:12:59.820
always being in the background

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:01.890
to having a moment to step out

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:03.270
and really shine on her own

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:05.940
and having belief from me and John.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:09.000
And unfortunately for John,
picking me as her coach,

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:09.870
- Unfortunately.

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:10.703
- Meant a lot.

00:13:10.703 --> 00:13:11.906
But she said, you know.

00:13:11.906 --> 00:13:12.739
- It was amazing.

00:13:12.739 --> 00:13:13.920
I said I have a lot to prove.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:14.760
I feel like you do too.

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:17.550
And that became our sort of connection.

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:18.720
That was a special moment.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:22.920
- The best block ever used in any season

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:25.473
was this season against him for Kenzie.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.290
- Mr. Mullet himself.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:31.045
- He literally looks like
he could be your nephew.

00:13:31.045 --> 00:13:32.760
(John laughing)

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:34.213
- [Blake] Poor kid, you just crushed him.

00:13:34.213 --> 00:13:36.029
- [John] He was like, he
was made to be on your team.

00:13:36.029 --> 00:13:38.037
- [Kelly] You just wait until
you see his song I gave him.

00:13:38.037 --> 00:13:39.720
- You crushed his chances.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:40.553
- [Kelly] Whatever.

00:13:40.553 --> 00:13:42.420
- He was made to be on your team.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.603
And she blocked you.

00:13:43.603 --> 00:13:44.640
- I do, I apologize

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:46.350
every time I see him, no kidding.

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:47.863
I go, I'm really sorry.

00:13:47.863 --> 00:13:49.680
I was like, I mean, I'm
kind of so glad I did it,

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.763
but I'm really sorry.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:52.583
Anyway.

00:13:52.583 --> 00:13:53.416
We're okay cowboy.

00:13:53.416 --> 00:13:55.440
What's your favorite
moment from this season?

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:59.430
- I like when I turned
around and it was Pete Morrow

00:13:59.430 --> 00:14:02.215
standing back there that I hadn't seen.

00:14:02.215 --> 00:14:05.760
For all I knew the guy was in
prison or dead or something.

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:09.240
Like I hadn't seen him in
that like 25 years, you know?

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.530
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.940
- And I didn't even recognize him.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:12.960
I mean like.

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:14.100
- No we're aware.

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:14.933
- [Blake] Huh?

00:14:14.933 --> 00:14:17.912
- We're aware that you
didn't recognize your friend.

00:14:17.912 --> 00:14:19.254
- I was like, that's not Pete.

00:14:19.254 --> 00:14:22.140
The Pete had, when I knew
him, he wore like the mobetta.

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:24.210
He had like a Garth hat.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:27.240
And then, now he's Pete, like that Pete.

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:28.830
I didn't recognize him, get over it.

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:30.240
- Oh my God, that was
actually my favorite.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:31.112
- It's going to happen
to you one of these days.

00:14:31.112 --> 00:14:31.945
And I can't wait.

00:14:31.945 --> 00:14:33.060
- My favorite moment was turning around

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:36.387
and realizing he was
supposed to know Pete.

00:14:37.355 --> 00:14:38.517
I was, I mean, I get it.

00:14:38.517 --> 00:14:40.110
You don't see each other for a long time,

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:41.053
but it was pretty funny.

00:14:41.053 --> 00:14:42.180
- I really liked Pete

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:44.910
and I was trying to get him
to join my team outta spite.

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:45.743
You know.

00:14:45.743 --> 00:14:46.950
- He wasn't doing it.

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:47.970
- No, no, no, no.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:49.680
And there's something, it's
the gravitational pull.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:50.850
It's annoying, I know.

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:54.030
What has been the best
thing about coaching so far?

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:56.370
- Other than just getting to know you all

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:58.860
and spend that time and laugh so hard.

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:00.870
I just love seeing the
talent that's on the show

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:04.560
and getting to know these
artists and work with them.

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:06.240
It's just like a really special experience

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:08.730
to be able to share some
of what we've learned

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:11.010
and been able to do in our
lives with these artists

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.840
that are just wanting
to do the same thing.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:14.490
It's this really special opportunity

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:16.650
to be able to share that with people,

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:18.120
to be in that position
is really interesting.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.179
It's just so cool to be there.

00:15:20.179 --> 00:15:22.080
And yeah, they're all so
nice and cool, I love them.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:23.550
I'm obsessed with my team.

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:24.636
I talk to them all the time.

00:15:24.636 --> 00:15:26.276
- You come home with your first team too.

00:15:26.276 --> 00:15:27.150
It's like, you get so obsessed.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:27.983
You love them all.

00:15:27.983 --> 00:15:29.430
But like your first, it's so exciting.

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:31.595
- I've broken every role in my contract.

00:15:31.595 --> 00:15:33.435
I've talked to them all, all the time.

00:15:33.435 --> 00:15:34.268
I'm like DMing them.

00:15:34.268 --> 00:15:35.490
They're like, you're
not supposed to do that.

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:37.027
And I'm like, sorry.

00:15:37.027 --> 00:15:38.670
(Kelly laughing)

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:40.500
- No, I know you're sending
stuff to the hotel for them.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.810
You're very, this is the
coolest thing about you though.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:45.090
I really hope people get to see from you.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:46.500
Like just working with you on the show.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:50.520
Like backstage, I have to
have my eye makeup redone,

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:52.650
like she's hysterical.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:54.810
She's so funny, very quick witted.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:55.740
I didn't know this about you.

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:56.573
I knew you were a talented,

00:15:56.573 --> 00:15:57.660
I knew you'd be a great coach.

00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:58.650
I knew all those things,

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:00.360
but I didn't know how funny you were

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.220
because we'd never really hung much.

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:03.180
- It' lifeless, I know.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:04.950
It seems totally made up.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:06.660
- We only see when we're watching it,

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:07.710
we only see like performing.

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.690
- For sure and like Seven
Rings, which is like, what?

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:10.740
Who is that, you know?

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.480
- Well, that's a great song.

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:13.313
- Thank you.

00:16:13.313 --> 00:16:14.146
But like, what does that mean?

00:16:14.146 --> 00:16:15.180
- That's like one of my favorites.

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:16.170
- You know what I mean,
that's not a person.

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.214
- It's not a person, she's a robot.

00:16:18.214 --> 00:16:19.500
- Punchline, you know what I mean.

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:20.640
- No, but you're hilarious.

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:21.840
And I thought it was so interesting

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:23.820
because usually it takes
coaches that come on,

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.260
like just being there for eight seasons,

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:26.760
it takes them a minute to like,

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:29.610
get used to being free with their words

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:30.900
and like their personality.

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:32.250
And you kind of like, right,

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:34.710
it was like, I think the second
or third day of the blinds,

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:36.930
you were like, nevermind, I'm here.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.370
And it was like, awesome.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:39.900
Did you find it nerve-wracking?

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:40.980
- It was a little nerve-wracking

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.470
but you all made me feel so comfortable

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:45.360
and are the nicest people

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:47.220
that I've met in this whole thing.

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:48.510
Like just the most fun ever.

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:49.710
And you made me feel so comfortable.

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:51.244
So it's because of you guys,

00:16:51.244 --> 00:16:52.077
you guys were push

00:16:52.077 --> 00:16:53.040
and also Blake was
pushing all the buttons.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:54.040
Sorry, I'll shut up.

00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:56.130
- But you know what though,

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:59.070
he does though because he feels able to.

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:00.819
That's when I feel like
it's the best chemistry.

00:17:00.819 --> 00:17:01.652
- That's helpful.

00:17:01.652 --> 00:17:02.485
- Yeah, it's helpful.

00:17:02.485 --> 00:17:03.420
It sets you up up for jokes.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:06.600
- It does, he gives you
a good setup every time.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.980
- [Kelly] Yeah, he just opens his mouth.

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:09.030
- Yes.

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:09.863
That's it.

00:17:09.863 --> 00:17:11.171
- Well, they act tough.
- [Ariana] He just walks in.

00:17:11.171 --> 00:17:13.620
- He just walks in and
there's a joke coming,

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:14.940
but Blake and John are,

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:16.800
they are terrified of you, look at this.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:18.600
- [Ariana] Oh?
- Yes.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:21.930
- Ariana has a huge fan base

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.700
and they are fervent.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:27.466
And if they show up to
vote, we're all in trouble.

00:17:27.466 --> 00:17:30.513
- 100%, are you scared at all?

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:32.250
- Now, what?

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:34.260
I'm not afraid of her fan
base, where are they at?

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:35.913
Look at me, where's the camera.

00:17:36.897 --> 00:17:38.430
Bring it on Ariana fans, bring it on.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:39.680
I'm not afraid of Ariana.

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:44.754
- He is so afraid of Ariana's fan base.

00:17:44.754 --> 00:17:46.410
(Kelly laughing and clapping)

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:47.243
Thoughts?

00:17:47.243 --> 00:17:48.300
We said this when you came in,

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:49.133
I mean, it was apparent.

00:17:49.133 --> 00:17:50.520
Literally the entire
audience was screaming

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:52.260
and we were like, we have no chance.

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:53.987
Like it was like, it was amazing.

00:17:53.987 --> 00:17:55.140
- I don't know that that's true.

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:56.013
- Well, I'm just saying like you have--

00:17:56.013 --> 00:17:58.050
- I do not think that that's true.

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:00.330
- But you're like a, you're a huge star.

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:01.654
I don't know.

00:18:01.654 --> 00:18:04.700
- What are you talking
about, Kelly Clarkson!

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:05.850
- No, I'm just saying,

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.782
it's one of those things
that you watch out.

00:18:08.782 --> 00:18:10.935
(audience clapping)

00:18:10.935 --> 00:18:13.143
No, it's so different.

00:18:13.143 --> 00:18:13.976
- Sorry.

00:18:13.976 --> 00:18:14.809
- Anyway, we're all,

00:18:14.809 --> 00:18:16.230
it's gotta feel a little good.

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:18.360
The little bit of competitiveness in you

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:20.250
has gotta be like, they're
all a little terrified.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:22.710
- I really don't think
that I have the chance

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:23.543
you think I have.

00:18:23.543 --> 00:18:25.290
- You can think all you
want, but it's true.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:26.610
- First of all.

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:27.660
Thank you.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.340
The beautiful thing about it is that

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:30.840
even just being on the show,

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.910
this is such a beautiful
chance for them to be seen

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:34.050
by the world in a new way.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:35.046
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:18:35.046 --> 00:18:36.437
- This is just us getting to meet them

00:18:36.437 --> 00:18:38.910
and give them this first chance.

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:39.930
And it's really special.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.700
Cause I think you're gonna
fall in love with all of them.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.653
I really do.
- They're so good.

00:18:43.653 --> 00:18:45.782
(audience clapping)

00:18:45.782 --> 00:18:49.710
- One of my favorite moments
of the whole season so far was

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:51.030
the coach performance.

00:18:51.030 --> 00:18:55.740
Because like just getting
to sing with this woman

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:57.660
and also Blake and John,

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:01.320
it was just such an incredible experience.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.660
Like the coolest part was
the rehearsal beforehand

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:05.610
where all of us were just
sitting around a piano

00:19:05.610 --> 00:19:08.130
and just like hearing
their voices in the room

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:09.000
was so special.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.530
Cause you're so familiar with their voices

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:12.000
because of their huge records.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.550
And you hear them all the time.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:15.473
- No, it was fun.

00:19:15.473 --> 00:19:16.470
It was my favorite part.
- [Ariana] It was so special.

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:18.148
- Yeah.
- [Ariana] What a cool memory.

00:19:18.148 --> 00:19:18.981
I was like, I gotta sing now.

00:19:18.981 --> 00:19:20.400
That's not fair, bye.

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:22.173
- Shut up, oh my God.
- Okay.

